course: dictionary
lesson: 5288
title: Jumpy: nervous, jerky or unsteady
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Jumpy has three meanings, and the context tells you which one to use. The most common meaning is nervous, or easily scared. «Everyone was jumpy after the strange noise.» A strange noise makes people feel on edge, so jumpy means nervous here.
explain: Jumpy can also describe movement that is not smooth. «Stop-motion looks jumpy if the camera moves» means the pictures jerk instead of flowing. A jumpy horse or cat is one that moves in sudden jerks and can startle at any moment.
explain: Jumpy can describe numbers too. A jumpy line on a graph rises and falls a lot instead of going steadily up, and jumpy prices go up and down quickly. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If nervous fits, use nervous.
fact: Jumpy means nervous and easily frightened or startled (informal).
fact: Jumpy also means moving in sudden jerks, not smooth, as in «a jumpy video».
fact: For money, jumpy means going up and down quickly and unpredictably, like prices.
fact: «Jittery» means shaky and jumpy, so it is a close synonym.
fact: You can check a meaning by swapping it into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Everyone was jumpy after the strange noise.» What does jumpy mean here? | Moving smoothly and slowly | *Nervous and easily startled | Very tired after a long day | Going up in price
exercise: «Stop-motion looks jumpy if the camera moves.» What does jumpy describe? | A loud, booming voice | A price that never changes | A happy, friendly person | *Movement in sudden jerks, not smooth
exercise: Prices on the market go up and down quickly and unpredictably. Which word fits best? | famished | *jumpy | ancient | curt
test: «The stoats, already jumpy from his morning trick, heard the uproar.» Which word is closest in meaning to jumpy here? | sleepy | *nervous | smooth | brave
test: Which word means about the same as jumpy, as in shaky and on edge? | *jittery | sleepy | calm | steady
exam: Which sentence uses jumpy with the money meaning? | *The jumpy share prices went up and down all day | The jumpy sea was calm and flat all morning | The jumpy child fell asleep in the car
